need to aggregate \"sold_products\" as products with sales in valid orders. If a product has order_items but order invalid, not counted. Good.\n\nNeed maybe using COUNT(DISTINCT pbm.product_id) for total products but if product brand map has historical noncurrent, filtered is_current. Good.\n\nNeed alias maybe \"total_products\", \"active_products\", \"sales\", \"sell_through_pct\". The problem uses \"商品总数、有效订单中动销商品数、不含运费商品销售额两位和动销率百分数两位\". Could use total_product_count, sold_product_count, sales_amount, sell_through_pct. Need output columns order: brand_id first then these. Good.\n\nNeed maybe use `ROUND(..., 2)` on SUM returns numeric? price numeric, SUM numeric, ROUND numeric fine. Ratio numeric: 100.0 * COUNT / NULLIF(COUNT,0) returns numeric? COUNT int, numeric; fine. `ROUND(...,2)` fine.\n\nPotential issue: HAVING sales known but if SUM(CASE...) = 0? Is 0 known? If price zero, sum 0 is known. HAVING SUM(...) IS NOT NULL includes 0. Good.\n\nPotential issue: The query use LEFT JOIN orders with condition, then SUM(CASE WHEN o.order_id IS NOT NULL THEN oi.price END). If an order is canceled, o null, no sum. Good. If order_item belongs to valid order, included. If order_item belongs to canceled and same product also valid, valid included.\n\nPotential issue: \"有效订单中动销商品数\" distinct product in valid orders. If a product has multiple mappings current to multiple brands, count per brand. Fine.\n\nNeed output only SQL, no explanation, no code fence. The system also says can add comment line. But hard rule direct output. We can just output SQL. Must be one SELECT. WITH is allowed? \"只输出一条SELECT\" might disallow WITH? It says only output one SELECT; CTE is a SELECT? Better use single SELECT no CTE to avoid issue. We'll use plain SELECT.\n\nNeed consider use of `COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN o.order_id IS NOT NULL THEN oi.product_id END)` counts valid order product. Good.\n\nLet's formulate:\n\nSELECT\n  pbm.brand_id,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT pbm.product_id) AS total_products,\n  CO